  "statement": {
    "text": "Water fills a cone (vertex down) at 2 m³/min. The cone has height = radius. When radius is 3m, how fast is the radius increasing?"
  },
  "objectives": [
    "Set up related rates problem",
    "Differentiate implicitly with respect to time"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "order": 1,
      "currentState": {
        "description": "Step 1"
      },
      "prompt": {
        "question": "Volume of cone: $V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h$. Given $h = r$, substitute",
        "hint": "$V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^3$"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^3$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$V = \\pi r^2 h$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2$"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Correct! Since $h = r$, we get $V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2(r) = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^3$",
          "insight": "Expressing V in terms of single variable r simplifies differentiation"
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "Remember to substitute $h = r$ into the volume formula",
          "2": "Don't forget the $\\frac{1}{3}$ coefficient for cone volume"
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Simplified volume formula"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "order": 2,
      "currentState": {
        "description": "Step 2"
      },
      "prompt": {
        "question": "Differentiate both sides with respect to time $t$",
        "hint": "$\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi \\cdot 3r^2 \\frac{dr}{dt}$"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\pi r^2 \\frac{dr}{dt}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\pi r^3$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$\\frac{dV}{dt} = 3\\pi r^2$"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Correct! Chain rule gives $\\frac{dV}{dt} = \\pi r^2 \\frac{dr}{dt}$",
          "insight": "Each variable that depends on time needs its derivative"
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "Missing $\\frac{dr}{dt}$ - remember to use chain rule",
          "2": "You need to differentiate, not just evaluate"
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Differentiated equation"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "order": 3,
      "currentState": {
        "description": "Step 3"
      },
      "prompt": {
        "question": "Substitute: $\\frac{dV}{dt} = 2$, $r = 3$, solve for $\\frac{dr}{dt}$",
        "hint": "$2 = \\pi(3)^2\\frac{dr}{dt}$"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{2}{9\\pi}$ m/min"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{2}{3\\pi}$ m/min"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{1}{9\\pi}$ m/min"
        }
      ],
      "correctOptionIndex": 0,
      "feedback": {
        "correct": {
          "explanation": "Correct! $\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{2}{9\\pi} \\approx 0.071$ m/min",
          "insight": "As radius increases, the rate of radius change decreases for constant volume rate"
        },
        "incorrect": {
          "1": "Remember $r = 3$, so $r^2 = 9$",
          "2": "Solve: $2 = 9\\pi \\frac{dr}{dt}$, so $\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{2}{9\\pi}$"
        }
      },
      "resultState": {
        "description": "Found rate of change"
      }
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "keyInsights": [
      "When $r = 3$m and $\\frac{dV}{dt} = 2$ m³/min, the radius increases at $\\frac{2}{9\\pi} \\approx 0.071$ m/min"
    ],
    "fullSolution": "$V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^3 \\Rightarrow \\frac{dV}{dt} = \\pi r^2\\frac{dr}{dt}$. With $r=3$, $\\frac{dV}{dt}=2$: $2 = 9\\pi\\frac{dr}{dt} \\Rightarrow \\frac{dr}{dt} = \\frac{2}{9\\pi}$ m/min",
